      <fr:mainmatter>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors>
              <fr:author>
                <fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link>
              </fr:author>
            </fr:authors>
            <fr:date>
              <fr:year>2025</fr:year>
              <fr:month>7</fr:month>
              <fr:day>14</fr:day>
            </fr:date>
            <fr:uri>https://kellenkanarios.com/C00V/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>C00V</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/C00V/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="Softmax">Softmax</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter><html:p>The softmax function <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathrm {softmax}: \mathbb {R}^d \to  \mathbb {R}^d]]></fr:tex> is defined by
<fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[\mathrm {softmax}(\mathbf {x})_i = \frac {e^{x_i}}{\sum _{j = 1}^{d} e^{x_j}}]]></fr:tex></html:p>
  
 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(110, 67, 101);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(110, 67, 101);">Claim.</html:span> 
  The Jacobian of the softmax function for <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathbf {y} = \mathrm {softmax}(\mathbf {x})]]></fr:tex> is given by
  <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
    \begin {align*}
      \frac {\partial  y_i}{\partial  x_j} = y_i(\delta _{ij} - y_j),
    \end {align*}
  ]]></fr:tex>
  or, in matrix form,
  <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
    \begin {align*}
      J = \mathrm {diag}(\mathbf {y}) - \mathbf {y}\mathbf {y}^\top .
    \end {align*}
  ]]></fr:tex>
</html:div>


  
  
 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(109, 103, 101);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(109, 103, 101);" /> 
  <html:details><html:summary><html:span class="foldout" style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(109, 103, 101);">Proof.</html:span></html:summary>
    Write <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[y_i = e^{x_i} / S]]></fr:tex> with <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[S = \sum _{k=1}^{d} e^{x_k}]]></fr:tex>, so that <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\partial  S / \partial  x_j = e^{x_j}]]></fr:tex>. By the quotient rule,
<fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
    \begin {align*}
      \frac {\partial  y_i}{\partial  x_j}
        &= \frac {\delta _{ij} e^{x_i} S - e^{x_i} e^{x_j}}{S^2} \\
        &= \delta _{ij}\frac {e^{x_i}}{S} - \frac {e^{x_i}}{S}\frac {e^{x_j}}{S} \\
        &= \delta _{ij} y_i - y_i y_j \\
        &= y_i(\delta _{ij} - y_j).
    \end {align*}
]]></fr:tex>
    Collecting these entries into a matrix, the diagonal contributes <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[y_i]]></fr:tex> along <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathrm {diag}(\mathbf {y})]]></fr:tex> and the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[-y_i y_j]]></fr:tex> term is the outer product <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathbf {y}\mathbf {y}^\top ]]></fr:tex>, giving <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[J = \mathrm {diag}(\mathbf {y}) - \mathbf {y}\mathbf {y}^\top ]]></fr:tex>.
</html:details>
</html:div>


</fr:mainmatter>
